          %h2#in_linear_algebra In linear algebra
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %strong line
            is the field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            over itself. More generally,
            %em a line
            is a vector space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
            to this, i.e. any 1-dimensional
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            models the naive intuition of the geometric line in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+geometry"} Euclidean geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line"} complex line
          %p
            In many contexts of modern mathematics, however,
            %em line
            implicitly refers to the complex line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            (which as a real vector space is the
            = succeed "!)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
          %h2#over_an_algebraic_theory Over an algebraic theory
          %p
            We discuss here how in the context of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+Lawvere+theory"} algebras over
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}_T
            which generalizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          %h3#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+category"} syntactic category
            of) any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            we have that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+conjugation"} Isbell conjugation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %msup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi Spec
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi 𝒪
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathcal{O} \dashv Spec)\colon
                  T Alg^{op} \stackrel{\overset{\mathcal{O}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{Spec}{\to}}
                  Sh(C)
          %p
            relates
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            over duals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi T
                  %msup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \hookrightarrow C \subset T Alg^{op}
            of
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical coverage
          %p
            By the
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory#FreeAlgebras"} free T-algebra adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi T
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi Alg
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi T
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi T
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (F_T \dashv U_T)\colon T Alg \stackrel{\overset{F_T}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U_T}
                  {\to}}
                  Set
          %p
            we have the free
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi TAlg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_T(*) \in TAlg
            on a single generator.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-line object
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mi T
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Spec
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{A}_T \coloneqq Spec F_T(*) \in Sh(C)
                    \\,.
          %h3#AdditiveGroupObject The additive group object
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜𝒷
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Ab}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
            of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ab
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒜𝒷
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ab\colon \mathcal{Ab} \to T
            of Lawvere theories is an
            = succeed "." do
              %strong abelian Lawvere theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ab
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi ab
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi Alg
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ab
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ab
                          %mo *
                  %mi Ab
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (ab_* \dashv ab^*)\colon
                  T Alg \stackrel{\overset{ab_*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{ab^*}{\to}}
